# Complexity budget (blinker convention)

`npm run lint` enforces these numbers as a ratchet (existing violations have
inline disables). There are still **no git hooks**, so a skipped lint will not
be caught locally. Stay inside the budget anyway:

- `complexity` (cyclomatic) ≤ 12
- `max-depth` (block nesting) ≤ 4
- `max-lines-per-function` ≤ 80
- `max-params` ≤ 5

New or edited code must comply. Do not disable a diagnostic to get a new big
function past review — extract instead.

## When you touch code here

- **Make it work, then make it right.** After the suite is green and before you
  ship, extract any function you pushed over budget. This is the Refactor leg of
  Red-Green-Refactor.
- **Don't accrete into orchestrators.** Bolting "one more branch / guard" onto a
  big function is how factories and dispatchers rot. Prefer a pipeline of named
  helpers over a deeper `if` tree.
- Mutation testing and CRAP have not landed (RD-24153). Do not wait for a
  coverage-quality score to tell you a function is too big — trust the budget.
